From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:35:52 +0000
Subject: feat(compose): add a canvas text primitive to DrawScope

Kuikly's DrawScope had no way to draw or measure text, so a Compose Canvas
could not render diagram labels even though every renderer's CanvasView
implements font/textAlign/fillText/strokeText/measureText. Porting the
Jetpack Compose drawText(TextMeasurer, ...) stack is not possible here: the
renderer shapes the text itself and never hands back a TextLayoutResult.

Add DrawScope.drawText(text, origin, style, alpha, drawStyle) and
DrawScope.measureText(text, style) as Kuikly-specific extensions with HTML
canvas semantics: origin is the alphabetic baseline point, style.textAlign
chooses which side of origin.x the run extends to, and TextStyle color,
fontSize (sp scaled by density, like the Text composable), fontWeight,
fontStyle and fontFamily are lowered to the renderer font command.
KuiklyCanvas sends font/textAlign only when they change within a bind and
converts pixels to the renderer's density-independent units.

Fork-Patch: compose-canvas-draw-text
Upstream-Status: submitted Tencent-TDS/KuiklyUI#1784

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>

